123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Anomaly detection focuses on identifying data samples that deviate from normal patterns. In many real-world applications, such as industrial inspection, medical imaging, and cybersecurity, anomalous samples are rare or not available during training. This makes supervised learning approaches ineffective and motivates the use of unsupervised methods.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Autoencoders are well-suited for this task because they learn to reconstruct normal data without requiring labeled anomalies. When trained only on normal samples, an autoencoder can accurately reconstruct normal patterns but produces higher reconstruction errors for anomalous inputs. This reconstruction error can therefore be used as a reliable anomaly score.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
125 0 obj
<<
