167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 265 0 R
/E (One of the main challenges observed in this project is the structural similarity between certain clothing categories. Anomalies that closely resemble T-shirts, such as pullovers and shirts, often resulted in lower reconstruction errors, making them harder to detect. This highlights a limitation of reconstruction-based anomaly detection methods when dealing with visually similar classes.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 266 0 R
/E (Another challenge is the trade-off between reconstruction quality and detection sensitivity. Architectures that are highly expressive, such as attention-based models, may unintentionally learn to reconstruct anomalous patterns, reducing their effectiveness as anomaly detectors.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
